By applying the formal asymptotic framework of two-scale expansions alongside Hu's lower bound method, we establish precise asymptotics for the first Robin eigenvalue of a nonlinear elliptic operator defined on a bounded open domain $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^n$. This approach accommodates the specific scenario where the nonlinear operator takes the form $|
abla u|^{p-2}
abla u + a(x) |u|^{p-2} u$, subject to the boundary condition $|
abla u|^{p-2}
u + \alpha(x) |u|^{p-2} = 0$ on $\partial\Omega$ with $p>2$. Furthermore, leveraging both asymptotic estimates and lower bound estimates yields a corresponding expansion for the corresponding eigenspace.
